@@ -0,0 +1,72 @@
+# ADR-0014: Experimental Sandbox and Evidence-Based Validation
+
+Status: Accepted — effective on owner-approved merge of this decision
+Owner: Catylist
+Date: 2026-10-26
+Decision authority: Donovan Worrell
+Amends: [Code of Conduct](../../CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md) 1.1.0 → 1.2.0, Law 7;
+[ADR-0000](ADR-0000-catylist-code-of-conduct.md), sections 4–5 and its sandbox-related rollout references;
+[ADR-0006](ADR-0006-default-branch-protection-and-signed-commits.md), rollout;
+[ADR-0010](ADR-0010-ring-0-input-gate-and-trust.md), rollout
+
+## Context and decision authority
+
+The decision authority directed: “Remove sandbox from the testbed requirements
+and mark experimental.” The named repository is `dlworrell/ruleset-sandbox`.
+This decision removes a mandatory repository dependency; it does not waive
+validation or change the requirement for owner approval and verified history.
+The change is prepared in a signed review PR and takes effect on its
+owner-approved merge. No machine or AI approval substitutes for that action.
+
+## Decision
+
+1. Classify `dlworrell/ruleset-sandbox` as **experimental** in the repository
+   inventory. It is optional exploratory work, not a required testbed, pilot,
+   release gate, qualification authority or prerequisite for other repos.
+2. Replace mandatory named-sandbox trials with recorded positive and refusal
+   cases using controlled fixtures or appropriate owning-repository evidence.
+   Record the exact source revision, expected behavior, observed result and
+   limits. A simulated result must not be presented as a live platform test.
+3. Preserve dry-run drift review, owner-approved application, verified commits,
+   merge-only history and exact-head checks. Experiments do not authorize a
+   new required check or a blanket rollout; applicable existing rollout and
+   acceptance evidence remains necessary.
+4. Experimental classification does not relax the repository's own baseline
+   protections. Ownership is project-owned and default-branch policy remains
+   `protected`. Historical sandbox evidence remains evidence about its original
+   subject; new sandbox success or availability is never an acceptance gate.
+5. AEMS may retain explicit optional experimental coverage. That is not
+   mandatory testbed enrollment and must not block other repository adoption.
+   This change does not silently enroll additional repositories or expand App
+   permissions. Normal per-repository ADR-0000 adoption remains required.
+
+## Implementation and migration
+
+The Code advances to 1.2.0 through this amendment. Catylist's ADR-0000 Code
+version pointer is updated; its historical body is preserved and the named
+sandbox requirements in its sections 4–5, implementation table, alternatives
+and follow-up are superseded by this decision. Downstream ADR-0000 version
+pointers change only through their ordinary reviewable adoption PRs; no
+downstream file is rewritten by this PR. Version-pointer rollout is distinct
+from accepting an experimental repo as production evidence.
+
+AEMS's operating procedure and coverage description identify the sandbox as
+an optional experiment. Existing in-memory unit fixtures whose sample repo
+name happens to contain `sandbox` remain offline fixtures; running them does
+not require that GitHub repository or access to it. No experiment is deleted.
+
+## Acceptance and recovery
+
+- Repository inventory, required-file and Markdown-link validation passes.
+- The sandbox inventory entry is experimental and retains protected policy.
+- The Code's Law 7 and active rollout procedures no longer require a named
+  sandbox. Historical evidence and superseded text remain distinguishable.
+- Owner governance approval and merge are recorded in the PR.
+- Downstream Code-version adoption remains an explicit follow-up, with
+  incomplete coverage reported as such.
+
+Rollback is another reviewed Catylist ADR and Code version change, not a
+history rewrite. Removing the sandbox dependency does not mark a failed test
+passing or establish product qualification.
+
+AI-assisted preparation by ChatGPT for @dlworrell.
